# Python
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Generated exports (regenerate anytime)
exports/*
!exports/.gitkeep

# OS junk
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NOT COMMITTED — and why
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Third-party manufacturer manuals (11 MB of PDFs).
# These are copyrighted vendor documents used as research inputs. The citations
# that matter are recorded per code in data/ and per brand in docs/sources/.
# Do not redistribute them in the repository.
research-raw/*.pdf
research-raw/*.doc
research-raw/*.docx
# Screenshots from vendor sites are kept: the two PNGs are our own captures of
# the reference UI. If a vendor-branded asset ever needs to go, delete it here.

# NOTE: app-pipeline/db/kb.sqlite, kb.json, brands.json, search-index.json and
# data-manifest.json ARE deliberately committed, even though build_kb.py can
# regenerate them.
#   - the app builder's first step is to copy kb.sqlite into the Android assets,
#     so a fresh clone must contain the exact validated database;
#   - CI_CD.md's "data is up to date" gate is a `git diff --exit-code`, which can
#     only work on tracked files;
#   - the build is reproducible (build_kb.py honours KB_BUILT_AT), so these are
#     never out of date by accident.
# The source of truth remains data/*.json. If you change data, rebuild and commit
# the app-pipeline artefacts in the same change.

# The Android app is a SEPARATE repository. Its own copy of the database lives at
# app/src/main/assets/db/kb.sqlite and is committed there. Never let the two
# drift apart: both must match the SHA-256 in app-pipeline/data-manifest.json.

# Android / Gradle (for when the app code joins this repo)
.gradle/
build/
local.properties
*.apk
*.aab
*.iml
.idea/
captures/
.externalNativeBuild/
.cxx/
*.hprof

# Editors
.vscode/
*.swp
*~
